# United Kingdom and Switzerland: bank holidays of England and Wales, the Bank of England's rate decisions, the UK
# consumer price index release, the holidays of the SIX Swiss Exchange and of the Swiss payment systems SIC and
# euroSIC, and the Swiss National Bank's December rate decision.
#
# Translated from holidays-events rules/catalog/uk_ch.yaml.
#
# How to read a rule: "rule <key> for <event> in <scope> = <dates> with kind = ... cites ...;" says on which days the
# event <event> happens for the market, country or institution <scope>. The part after "=" is a date expression that
# is evaluated once per year: "25 DEC" is 25 December, "EASTER + 1D" the day after Easter Sunday, "1 MON MAY" the
# first Monday of May, "LAST MON AUG" the last Monday of August, "{SAT + 2D, SUN + 1D}" moves a date that falls on a
# Saturday by two days and one on a Sunday by one day, "> NEXT WED" moves to the next Wednesday strictly after the
# date (so "16 JAN - 1D > NEXT WED" is the Wednesday on or after 16 January), "> PRECEDING ON country:GB" moves a
# date that is not a business day in the UK calendar to the business day before. Rules only project: the dates an
# authority publishes are data that replace a rule's dates for that year, and dates that are only ever published have
# no rule. "kind = closed" marks a day on which the market or institution is shut; "kind = event" marks a dated event
# (a decision, a release) that does not change whether the day is a business day. "cites" names the source the rule
# is taken from; "label official" means that source is the authority itself. The full syntax is in README.md in this
# directory. Weekends are declared in weekends.rules (all scopes here have the Saturday-Sunday weekend).
#
# Scopes used in this file:
#   statistics_office:ONS       Office for National Statistics, the UK's national statistics office (Europe/London).
#   country:GB                  United Kingdom, country; the rules here are the bank holidays of England and Wales,
#                               which are also the holidays of the London markets (Europe/London).
#   central_bank:BOE            Bank of England, the UK's central bank; its Monetary Policy Committee sets Bank Rate.
#   exchange:XSWX               SIX Swiss Exchange, Zurich, stock exchange (market identifier code XSWX).
#   settlement_system:SIC       SIC (Swiss Interbank Clearing), the real-time gross settlement system for Swiss
#                               francs, run by SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd for the Swiss National Bank.
#   settlement_system:EUROSIC   euroSIC, the Swiss settlement system for euro payments, also run by SIX Interbank
#                               Clearing Ltd; it follows the closing days of the euro area's TARGET system.
#   central_bank:SNB            Swiss National Bank, Switzerland's central bank.


# ===================================================================================================================
# Office for National Statistics (statistics_office:ONS)
# ===================================================================================================================

# UK consumer price inflation: the monthly release of the consumer price index (CPI) by the Office for National
# Statistics, published at 07:00 UK time. The ONS announces each release date in its release calendar (an iCal feed;
# a date counts once its status is "confirmed"); those announced dates always win. For months it has not announced
# yet, the date is projected: the Wednesday on or after the 16th of the month. This is an observed pattern, not an
# ONS statement: the release is always on a Wednesday, usually the first Wednesday on or after the 16th; 43 of 53
# releases from September 2022 to January 2027 hit that day exactly, and all were within a week of it. The release
# does not close any market, so the day stays a business day.
rule ons.cpi for uk_cpi in statistics_office:ONS
  = [16 JAN : 1M : 16 DEC] - 1D > NEXT WED
  with kind = event, session 07:00 tz "Europe/London", note "Dates from the ONS release calendar, projected beyond it"
  cites "ONS release calendar (iCal), Office for National Statistics" url "https://www.ons.gov.uk/calendar/releasecalendar" label official;


# ===================================================================================================================
# United Kingdom: bank holidays of England and Wales (country:GB)
# The UK government publishes them on GOV.UK (source govuk_bank_holidays, a JSON feed); bank holidays are set by the
# Banking and Financial Dealings Act 1971 and by royal proclamation. On these days UK banks and the London markets
# are closed.
# ===================================================================================================================

# New Year's Day, 1 January. If it falls on a Saturday the bank holiday is the following Monday (3 January); if it
# falls on a Sunday, the following Monday (2 January).
rule gb.new_years_day for new_years_day in country:GB = 1 JAN {SAT + 2D, SUN + 1D}
  with kind = closed
  cites "GOV.UK bank holidays JSON, UK Government" url "https://www.gov.uk/bank-holidays.json" label official;

# Good Friday, the Friday two days before Easter Sunday (Western, Gregorian Easter).
rule gb.good_friday for good_friday in country:GB = EASTER - 2D
  with kind = closed
  cites "GOV.UK bank holidays JSON, UK Government" url "https://www.gov.uk/bank-holidays.json" label official;

# Easter Monday, the day after Easter Sunday (a bank holiday in England, Wales and Northern Ireland, not in Scotland).
rule gb.easter_monday for easter_monday in country:GB = EASTER + 1D
  with kind = closed
  cites "GOV.UK bank holidays JSON, UK Government" url "https://www.gov.uk/bank-holidays.json" label official;

# Early May bank holiday: the first Monday of May. (In 2020 it was moved by proclamation to Friday 8 May for the
# 75th anniversary of VE Day, and in 2023 an extra holiday was added for the coronation; such one-off changes come
# from the announcements, see gb.one_off below, and are not part of this rule.)
rule gb.early_may_bank_holiday for early_may_bank_holiday in country:GB = 1 MON MAY
  with kind = closed
  cites "GOV.UK bank holidays JSON, UK Government" url "https://www.gov.uk/bank-holidays.json" label official;

# Spring bank holiday: the last Monday of May. (In 2022 it was moved by proclamation to Thursday 2 June for the
# Queen's Platinum Jubilee; such one-off moves come from the announcements and are not part of this rule.)
rule gb.spring_bank_holiday for spring_bank_holiday in country:GB = LAST MON MAY
  with kind = closed
  cites "GOV.UK bank holidays JSON, UK Government" url "https://www.gov.uk/bank-holidays.json" label official;

# Summer bank holiday: the last Monday of August (England, Wales and Northern Ireland; Scotland has its own on the
# first Monday of August, not covered here).
rule gb.summer_bank_holiday for summer_bank_holiday in country:GB = LAST MON AUG
  with kind = closed
  cites "GOV.UK bank holidays JSON, UK Government" url "https://www.gov.uk/bank-holidays.json" label official;

# Christmas Day, 25 December. If it falls on Saturday or Sunday the bank holiday moves to the next free weekday:
# Saturday -> Monday 27, Sunday -> Tuesday 27, because Boxing Day takes Monday 26. Both cases are two days later.
rule gb.christmas_day for christmas_day in country:GB = 25 DEC {SAT + 2D, SUN + 2D}
  with kind = closed
  cites "GOV.UK bank holidays JSON, UK Government" url "https://www.gov.uk/bank-holidays.json" label official;

# Boxing Day, 26 December. If it falls on a Saturday the bank holiday is Monday 28 (Christmas Day takes Monday 27);
# if it falls on a Sunday, Tuesday 28 (Christmas Day is on Saturday 25 and its bank holiday takes Monday 27). Both
# cases are two days later.
rule gb.boxing_day for boxing_day in country:GB = 26 DEC {SAT + 2D, SUN + 2D}
  with kind = closed
  cites "GOV.UK bank holidays JSON, UK Government" url "https://www.gov.uk/bank-holidays.json" label official;

# One-off bank holidays, such as a coronation or a state funeral (for example 19 September 2022, the state funeral
# of Queen Elizabeth II, and 8 May 2023, the coronation of King Charles III). They are declared by royal
# proclamation, usually months ahead, and then appear in the GOV.UK bank holiday list. They cannot be predicted, so
# there are no dates until they are announced. The catalog files them under the event "unscheduled market
# disruption", which is a dated event rather than a closure class, hence kind = event here; in reality an announced
# one-off bank holiday closes UK banks and the London markets for the whole day.
# No rule: the dates are only announced (govuk_bank_holidays); they are data for the evaluator, under the key
# gb.one_off.


# ===================================================================================================================
# Bank of England (central_bank:BOE)
# ===================================================================================================================

# Bank of England Monetary Policy Committee (MPC) decision on Bank Rate. The MPC meets eight times a year; the Bank
# publishes provisional dates about a year ahead on its "upcoming MPC dates" page, and those announced dates always
# win. Beyond the published schedule four of the eight dates are projected from an observed pattern: the first
# Thursday of February and of November (right in all 14 cases from 2021 to 2027) and the third Thursday of March and
# of December (6 of 7 each). If such a Thursday is not a UK business day, the business day before it is taken. The
# other four meetings (May, June, August, September) moved between years in 2021-2023 and 2026, so they are not
# projected at all; they appear only once the Bank announces them. A decision does not close any market.
rule boe.mpc_decision for boe_decision in central_bank:BOE
  = 1 THU FEB > PRECEDING ON country:GB, 1 THU NOV > PRECEDING ON country:GB,
         3 THU MAR > PRECEDING ON country:GB, 3 THU DEC > PRECEDING ON country:GB
  with kind = event, note "Provisional dates published about a year ahead; only the February, March, November and December slots are projected"
  cites "Bank of England MPC dates, Bank of England" url "https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy/upcoming-mpc-dates" label official;


# ===================================================================================================================
# SIX Swiss Exchange (exchange:XSWX)
# Exchange holidays as published by SIX Group in its yearly trading calendar (source six_holidays, a PDF; the 2026
# calendar lists 1-2 Jan, 3 and 6 Apr, 1, 14 and 25 May, 24, 25 and 31 Dec). No trading on these days. The dates are
# fixed and are not moved when they fall on a weekend (the exchange is closed then anyway).
# ===================================================================================================================

# New Year's Day, 1 January.
rule xswx.new_years_day for new_years_day in exchange:XSWX = 1 JAN
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX trading / currency holiday calendar, SIX Group" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html" label official;

# Berchtold's Day (Berchtoldstag), 2 January, a traditional Swiss holiday observed in many cantons.
rule xswx.berchtolds_day for berchtolds_day in exchange:XSWX = 2 JAN
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX trading / currency holiday calendar, SIX Group" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html" label official;

# Good Friday, two days before Easter Sunday.
rule xswx.good_friday for good_friday in exchange:XSWX = EASTER - 2D
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX trading / currency holiday calendar, SIX Group" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html" label official;

# Easter Monday, the day after Easter Sunday.
rule xswx.easter_monday for easter_monday in exchange:XSWX = EASTER + 1D
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX trading / currency holiday calendar, SIX Group" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html" label official;

# Labour Day, 1 May (a holiday in Zurich and several other cantons).
rule xswx.labour_day for labour_day in exchange:XSWX = 1 MAY
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX trading / currency holiday calendar, SIX Group" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html" label official;

# Ascension Day, the Thursday 39 days after Easter Sunday.
rule xswx.ascension_day for ascension_day in exchange:XSWX = EASTER + 39D
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX trading / currency holiday calendar, SIX Group" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html" label official;

# Whit Monday, the Monday 50 days after Easter Sunday (the day after Pentecost).
rule xswx.whit_monday for whit_monday in exchange:XSWX = EASTER + 50D
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX trading / currency holiday calendar, SIX Group" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html" label official;

# Swiss National Day, 1 August, the federal holiday.
rule xswx.swiss_national_day for swiss_national_day in exchange:XSWX = 1 AUG
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX trading / currency holiday calendar, SIX Group" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html" label official;

# Christmas Eve, 24 December: the exchange is closed (an exchange holiday, not a public holiday; the SIC payment
# system stays open).
rule xswx.christmas_eve for christmas_eve in exchange:XSWX = 24 DEC
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX trading / currency holiday calendar, SIX Group" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html" label official;

# Christmas Day, 25 December.
rule xswx.christmas_day for christmas_day in exchange:XSWX = 25 DEC
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX trading / currency holiday calendar, SIX Group" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html" label official;

# St Stephen's Day (Boxing Day), 26 December.
rule xswx.boxing_day for boxing_day in exchange:XSWX = 26 DEC
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX trading / currency holiday calendar, SIX Group" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html" label official;

# New Year's Eve, 31 December: the exchange is closed (an exchange holiday, not a public holiday; the SIC payment
# system stays open).
rule xswx.new_years_eve for new_years_eve in exchange:XSWX = 31 DEC
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX trading / currency holiday calendar, SIX Group" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/market-data/news-tools/trading-currency-holiday-calendar.html" label official;


# ===================================================================================================================
# SIC, the Swiss franc payment system (settlement_system:SIC)
# Days without Swiss franc settlement: the Swiss bank holidays. The operator, SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd, publishes a
# clearing day calendar (source six_clearing_days, a CSV file refreshed daily) that holds only the forthcoming days,
# about a year ahead. These rules cover the past and the years beyond that file; where the file has data, its days
# replace these rules. Cross-check: ICE Clear Europe's Swiss franc holidays for 2026 are 1-2 Jan, 3 and 6 Apr, 1, 14
# and 25 May and 25 Dec. Unlike the exchange, SIC is open on 24 and 31 December. The dates are fixed and not moved
# when they fall on a weekend.
# ===================================================================================================================

# New Year's Day, 1 January.
rule sic.new_years_day for new_years_day in settlement_system:SIC = 1 JAN
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# Berchtold's Day, 2 January.
rule sic.berchtolds_day for berchtolds_day in settlement_system:SIC = 2 JAN
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# Good Friday, two days before Easter Sunday.
rule sic.good_friday for good_friday in settlement_system:SIC = EASTER - 2D
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# Easter Monday, the day after Easter Sunday.
rule sic.easter_monday for easter_monday in settlement_system:SIC = EASTER + 1D
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# Labour Day, 1 May.
rule sic.labour_day for labour_day in settlement_system:SIC = 1 MAY
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# Ascension Day, the Thursday 39 days after Easter Sunday.
rule sic.ascension_day for ascension_day in settlement_system:SIC = EASTER + 39D
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# Whit Monday, the Monday 50 days after Easter Sunday.
rule sic.whit_monday for whit_monday in settlement_system:SIC = EASTER + 50D
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# Swiss National Day, 1 August.
rule sic.swiss_national_day for swiss_national_day in settlement_system:SIC = 1 AUG
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# Christmas Day, 25 December.
rule sic.christmas_day for christmas_day in settlement_system:SIC = 25 DEC
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# St Stephen's Day (Boxing Day), 26 December.
rule sic.boxing_day for boxing_day in settlement_system:SIC = 26 DEC
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;


# ===================================================================================================================
# euroSIC, the Swiss euro payment system (settlement_system:EUROSIC)
# euroSIC follows the closing days of TARGET, the euro area's payment system run by the Eurosystem: New Year's Day,
# Good Friday, Easter Monday, 1 May, Christmas Day and 26 December. Swiss-only holidays (2 January, Ascension, Whit
# Monday, 1 August) are euroSIC business days. As for SIC, the operator's clearing day calendar (six_clearing_days)
# replaces these rules where it has data. The dates are fixed and not moved when they fall on a weekend.
# ===================================================================================================================

# New Year's Day, 1 January.
rule eurosic.new_years_day for new_years_day in settlement_system:EUROSIC = 1 JAN
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# Good Friday, two days before Easter Sunday.
rule eurosic.good_friday for good_friday in settlement_system:EUROSIC = EASTER - 2D
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# Easter Monday, the day after Easter Sunday.
rule eurosic.easter_monday for easter_monday in settlement_system:EUROSIC = EASTER + 1D
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# Labour Day, 1 May.
rule eurosic.labour_day for labour_day in settlement_system:EUROSIC = 1 MAY
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# Christmas Day, 25 December.
rule eurosic.christmas_day for christmas_day in settlement_system:EUROSIC = 25 DEC
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;

# St Stephen's Day (Boxing Day), 26 December.
rule eurosic.boxing_day for boxing_day in settlement_system:EUROSIC = 26 DEC
  with kind = closed
  cites "SIX Interbank Clearing clearing day calendar (SIC, SIC IP, euroSIC), SIX Interbank Clearing Ltd" url "https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/interbank-clearing/online-services/clearing-day-calendar.html" label official;


# ===================================================================================================================
# Swiss National Bank (central_bank:SNB)
# ===================================================================================================================

# Swiss National Bank quarterly monetary policy assessment (its rate decision), announced at 09:30 Swiss time. The
# SNB publishes the dates itself, yearly; those announced dates always win. It holds assessments in March, June,
# September and December. Only the December one follows a stable pattern and is projected beyond the published
# schedule: the Thursday on or after 10 December (right in 18 of 19 years from 2009 to 2027; 2020 was the exception).
# The March, June and September dates move between years and appear only once the SNB announces them. A decision does
# not close any market.
rule snb.assessment for snb_decision in central_bank:SNB
  = 10 DEC - 1D > NEXT THU
  with kind = event, session 09:30 tz "Europe/Zurich", note "Only the December assessment is projected"
  cites "SNB monetary policy assessment dates, Swiss National Bank" url "https://www.snb.ch/" label official;


# =====================================================================================================================
# subdivision:CH_ZRH - City of Zurich (D-220)
# Who sets it: the city council (Sechseläuten date rule of 1952); both customs are local afternoon holidays, not cantonal or
# federal ones. SIX and SIC operate normally.
# =====================================================================================================================

# Sechseläuten, Zurich's spring custom: work stops at midday, the afternoon is a local holiday. The third Monday of April;
# when that Monday falls in Holy Week the second Monday instead, and when it is Easter Monday the fourth Monday
# (Stadtratsbeschluss Nr. 1214 of 13 June 1952). The first item is the usual third Monday unless it is Holy Week Monday
# (Easter - 6 days) or Easter Monday; the second item gives the second Monday when the third one is Holy Week Monday
# (then Easter - 13 days is a Monday from 8 to 14 April); the third gives the fourth Monday when the third one is Easter
# Monday (then Easter + 8 days is a Monday from 22 to 28 April).
rule zrh.sechselaeuten for sechselaeuten in subdivision:CH_ZRH
  = 3 MON APR \ {EASTER - 6D, EASTER + 1D}, EASTER - 13D IF DAY 8..14 APR, EASTER + 8D IF DAY 22..28 APR
  with kind = short_day, note "afternoon only; no closing time stated"
  cites "City of Zurich customs (Sechseläuten, Knabenschiessen)" art "Stadtratsbeschluss Nr. 1214 of 13 June 1952" url "https://www.stadt-zuerich.ch/de/stadtleben/stadtportraet/zuerichs-geschichte/stadtarchiv/wissensportal/zuercher-sechselaeuten.html" label official;

# Knabenschiessen, Zurich's autumn shooting contest, held on the second weekend of September; the Monday afternoon is
# the city's holiday: the Monday after the second Sunday of September.
rule zrh.knabenschiessen for knabenschiessen in subdivision:CH_ZRH = 2 SUN SEP + 1D
  with kind = short_day, note "afternoon only; no closing time stated"
  cites "City of Zurich customs (Sechseläuten, Knabenschiessen)" url "https://www.stadt-zuerich.ch/de/stadtleben/stadtportraet/zuerichs-geschichte/stadtarchiv/wissensportal/zuercher-sechselaeuten.html" label official;
